cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "dominican-open-data-mcp: an MCP server for datos.gob.do"
message: >-
  If you use this software, or figures obtained through it, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alberto
    family-names: Castillo Aroca
    alias: alcastaro
    affiliation: >-
      OLDS — Observatorio Latinoamericano de Desarrollo Sostenible
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/alcastaro/datos.gob.do-MCP-server"
url: "https://github.com/alcastaro/datos.gob.do-MCP-server"
abstract: >-
  A Model Context Protocol server that turns the Dominican Republic's official
  open data portal, datos.gob.do, into a native integration for any MCP client.
  It exposes 1,061 datasets from 266 government institutions as typed tools,
  read-only resources and reusable prompts, and answers with the provenance a
  figure needs to be checked by a third party: the digest of the bytes it read,
  the query it ran, and what any numeric coercion excluded. Reachability is
  reported rather than assumed, because roughly half the catalog's files are
  refused by the publishing institutions' own sites.
keywords:
  - model context protocol
  - mcp
  - open data
